INGREDIENTS-

soked chana which is then boiled

3-4 medium size kande(check -quantity) for 1 big wati channa(white, unsoked, soke kelayavar becomes more than 1 wati),
8-10 lasoon
2-3cm ala
thodusa suka khobra(about 1tbs) {optional}take tikhat halad 

3-4 tomato
1-2 hirvi mirchi(adjustable)
grind these seperately, ok even if u grate them both

Take tikhat(ek chamcha, adjustable), halad(pav chamcha), dhane pood (2 chamche), jeere pud(1 chamcha) in a wati.
put water nd make a paste(so that it does not burn in the oil)


Process'
1. Take all ingredients, grind them in a mixer.
2. Take kadhai put tel, put one tamaalpatra(even idk what that is).
3. add jeere(pav chamcha)
4. add the masala paste.
5. paratofy for about 1 min
6. add the kanda wali paste
7. paratofy for 3-4 min
8. add tomato wali paste.
9. paratofy until tel sute
10. from the boiled chane, take out a tiny but of chana(about 1tbs), keep it aside, mash it 
11. take boiled chana, then remove water(keep water aside in summin), add only boiled channe in the kadhai nd masala
12 bhajofy chane for 3-4 mins [paratna nd bhaajna is same*]
13. add the water which we had removed from chane earlier acc to needed consistency
14. add the chana paste we had made 
15. mix it, add namak(swaadanusaar), add kitched king masala
16. if needed, add fresh cream or doodh chi saai(ew),or milk or khawaa {if u don't want masala ki taste or to make it a bit less maseledaar} (ok if not done, aai puts)
17. let it boil
18. enjoy

